{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And Aaron shall wave, etc., as a wave-offering.</b> He mentioned תנופה three times in this section: 'And Aaron shall wave the Levites as a wave-offering before YHWH,' and it is written 'and you shall wave them as a wave-offering to YHWH,' and it is written 'and you shall wave them as a wave-offering.' And Rashi explained: corresponding to the sons of Kohath, the sons of Gershon, and the sons of Merari. The first wave-offering corresponds to the sons of Kohath — therefore it says of it, 'and they shall be for doing the service of YHWH,' for the sons of Kohath are the bearers of the sanctuary, the consecrated things — the Ark and the Table and the Menorah and the Altars — and it is written (Numbers 7:7) ״כי עבודת הקדש עליהם״. The second corresponds to the sons of Gershon — therefore it says of it 'a wave-offering to YHWH,' for they too bore the curtains of the planks, which are seen in the Holy of Holies, and the service of the sanctuary is upon them as well. The third corresponds to the sons of Merari, who bore the planks of the Tabernacle and its bars and its pillars and its sockets, which are the vessels of copper and the wood; and of them it says תנופה without qualification, and did not mention 'before YHWH' or 'to YHWH,' for their ranks are distinguished one from another. And we find at the end of the section that he mentioned concerning the entirety of the Levites: 'And Aaron shall wave them as a wave-offering before YHWH,' in order to teach you that all of them are worthy and beloved before Him. And what it says, 'given, given they are to Me' — its explanation is: given for the labor of bearing, given for song; or one may say that because they gave their lives over the matter of the Calf, 'given they are to Me' — and from this Onkelos's translation: מסירין יהיבין.'"], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:30:50.109740850Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}